# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment variables
#
# Frontend (Vite) - only variables prefixed with VITE_ reach the browser bundle.
#
#   VITE_DATA_BACKEND   "api"   -> talk to the /api functions (Neon Postgres)
#                       "local" -> localStorage fallback, development only
#                       unset   -> "api" in a production build, "local" in `vite dev`
#
# Serverless functions (api/) - read from process.env on the host. These are
# NEVER exposed to the browser and must NOT be prefixed with VITE_.
#
#   DATABASE_URL        Neon POOLED connection string (host contains `-pooler`).
#                       Use the pooled endpoint, not the direct one: functions
#                       open a connection each and would exhaust a direct
#                       endpoint's connection limit almost immediately.
#
# SECURITY: nothing in this file may be a VITE_-prefixed database credential.
# Anything with that prefix is inlined into the public JavaScript bundle, where
# every visitor can read it. The browser must only ever call /api.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Frontend - leave unset to use the defaults above.
# VITE_DATA_BACKEND=

# Serverless functions - set these on the host, not in the repository.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@ep-xxx-pooler.REGION.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require

# Admin login for the test scripts (scripts/test-api.mjs, scripts/check-admin.mjs).
# Set them in the local, gitignored .env.local - never commit real values, the
# repository is public and this is a live admin account.
# IDCMS_ADMIN_EMAIL=
# IDCMS_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
